From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: fix RTL8261 1G speed reporting

The rtl8261x_read_status() we carry ran genphy_c45_read_status()
first and only then read the 1000BASE-T link-partner status, gated on
phydev->autoneg_complete, before a second phy_resolve_aneg_linkmode().
With a 1G-only link partner the resolve found no common linkmode and
left phydev->speed at SPEED_UNKNOWN on an up link, so ethtool and the
netdev LED trigger reported an unknown speed ("No phy led trigger
registered for speed(-1)").

Adopt the rtl8261x_read_status() body from the upstream net-next v10
revision: read the 1000BASE-T link-partner status into lp_advertising 
up front (gated on genphy_c45_aneg_done()) so genphy_c45_read_status()'s
own resolve sees the 1G ability.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -531,26 +531,27 @@ static int rtl8261x_get_features(struct
 
 static int rtl8261x_read_status(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
-	int ret;
+	int ret, val = 0;
+
+	if (phydev->autoneg == AUTONEG_ENABLE) {
+		ret = genphy_c45_aneg_done(phydev);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+
+		if (ret) {
+			val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2,
+					   RTL822X_VND2_C22_REG(MII_STAT1000));
+			if (val < 0)
+				return val;
+		}
+	}
+
+	mii_stat1000_mod_linkmode_lpa_t(phydev->lp_advertising, val);
 
 	ret = genphy_c45_read_status(phydev);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (phydev->autoneg == AUTONEG_ENABLE && phydev->autoneg_complete) {
-		int lp_status;
-
-		lp_status = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2,
-					 RTL822X_VND2_C22_REG(MII_STAT1000));
-		if (lp_status < 0)
-			return lp_status;
-
-		if (lp_status & (LPA_1000FULL | LPA_1000HALF)) {
-			mii_stat1000_mod_linkmode_lpa_t(phydev->lp_advertising, lp_status);
-			phy_resolve_aneg_linkmode(phydev);
-		}
-	}
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
